+
+**Verified clean:**
+
+- **Correctness** — reverse Dijkstra unchanged structurally; `w` computed once per popped node (`engine/routing.go:188`), lazy-deletion guarded by `done[]`, strict `<` relaxation keeps first-order choice. The diamond fixture genuinely discriminates: via-b cost ≈ 23.7 s vs via-c ≈ 15.7 s under time weights (b wins 152 m vs 452 m under length), with a wide margin — no float-tie fragility. Test mirrors the established `routeForkSpec` pattern exactly.
+- **Determinism** — weight is still a pure per-lane function; division is IEEE-deterministic and the divide-then-add shape isn't FMA-fusible, so no cross-platform contraction risk. Heap tie-break (lower index) and fixed pred order untouched. The ADR claim "runs without Route intents are bit-identical" holds: `routeNextHop` (engine.go:803) short-circuits on nil dest, and the table cache is derived state outside the CRC.
